WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.093 --> 00:00:05.375
Ally raced into the diner, determined to not let another fib get out of control.

2
00:00:05.376 --> 00:00:10.076
She had to explain to Ray that there had been a misunderstanding about the surprise party.

3
00:00:10.077 --> 00:00:13.649
But Ray was busy talking on the phone.

4
00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:23.325
"I don't want to interrupt him," Ally thought. "I'll explain all this later at home."

5
00:00:23.326 --> 00:00:30.422
After she and Barry were done collecting signatures for the petition, Ally headed home.

6
00:00:30.423 --> 00:00:40.764
"Alpha is still mad at me. I have to talk to her about things too," Ally thought.

7
00:00:40.765 --> 00:00:46.666
In her room she booted Alpha up. "Hi, Alpha, I'm home."

8
00:00:46.667 --> 00:00:50.426
Alpha made a snorting sound.

9
00:00:50.427 --> 00:00:55.509
"I know you're still mad at me, and I'm really sorry," Ally said.

10
00:00:55.510 --> 00:01:00.439
"The fibs I've told have gotten out of control and caused lots of trouble."

11
00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:02.571
"Humans fib because they can.

12
00:01:02.572 --> 00:01:07.149
They do not possess mind-reading abilities like Astralians," Alpha said.

13
00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:10.088
"Fibs can easily get out of control."

14
00:01:10.089 --> 00:01:13.022
"I know that now," Ally said.

15
00:01:13.023 --> 00:01:18.417
"I thought if no one got hurt, then telling fibs wasn't a bad thing.

16
00:01:18.418 --> 00:01:23.090
But I realize you can't always know who your fibs will hurt."

17
00:01:23.091 --> 00:01:27.692
"Affirmative." Alpha's tone softened. "It is clear you meant well.

18
00:01:27.693 --> 00:01:32.977
However, logic dictates you must tell the truth to everyone you have fibbed to."

19
00:01:32.978 --> 00:01:38.908
Ally nodded. "Let's see . . . Who have I fibbed to?

20
00:01:38.909 --> 00:01:49.256
Kate, Julius, Ray, sort of, and this doesn't even include all the people I've hidden my real identity from—"

21
00:01:49.257 --> 00:01:55.412
"Correction," Alpha interrupted. "It would be unwise to expose your Astralian identity."

22
00:01:55.413 --> 00:01:59.219
"But isn't pretending to be human a kind of fib?"

23
00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:02.381
"There are some truths that could endanger you.

24
00:02:02.382 --> 00:02:07.092
Some fibs are told out of necessity, but you must choose wisely."

25
00:02:07.093 --> 00:02:17.152
Ally groaned. "I'm still confused, but maybe that's what Mateo meant when he said some fibs are harmless."

26
00:02:17.153 --> 00:02:20.486
"Affirmative."

27
00:02:20.487 --> 00:02:24.969
"Thank you for helping me, Alpha. Okay, I'm going to do it!

28
00:02:24.970 --> 00:02:28.707
I'm going to tell the truth to everyone I've fibbed to.

29
00:02:28.708 --> 00:02:35.059
But first I have to bring the letters to Mayor Clark and try to fix this mess with the soccer field."

30
00:02:35.060 --> 00:02:41.019
Ally was about to put Alpha in her pocket when she noticed she had a voicemail message.

31
00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:46.485
"Oh! Lainie called today," Ally said. "She finally called me back."

32
00:02:46.486 --> 00:02:48.413
Ally hit Play.

33
00:02:48.414 --> 00:02:55.836
"Hi, Ally. Please call me back about the P.O.D. as soon as you can."

34
00:02:55.837 --> 00:02:59.672
"Quick, Alpha," Ally commanded. "Call Lainie."

35
00:02:59.673 --> 00:03:03.652
The phone rang twice before the call went to Lainie's voicemail.

36
00:03:03.653 --> 00:03:08.037
Ally left a message. "Hi, Lainie. I'm sorry I missed your call.

37
00:03:08.038 --> 00:03:14.001
Please call me back as soon as you can. I'm so excited to blast off with you!"

38
00:03:14.002 --> 00:03:20.913
Ally hung up and got ready to head into town. "It's time to get back to work!"

39
00:03:20.914 --> 00:03:24.565
Ally arrived at the mayor's office a little while later.

40
00:03:24.566 --> 00:03:29.036
"May I please speak with the mayor?" Ally asked the mayor's assistant.

41
00:03:29.037 --> 00:03:32.417
"She's in a meeting," the assistant said.

42
00:03:32.418 --> 00:03:40.809
"I can wait," Ally said. "It's very important."

43
00:03:40.810 --> 00:03:45.629
Ally waited for almost an hour before the mayor's door opened.

44
00:03:45.630 --> 00:03:49.366
Mayor Clark walked out with two men carrying blueprints.

45
00:03:49.367 --> 00:03:53.265
"We're excited for you to get to work!" she said to the men.

46
00:03:53.266 --> 00:03:56.442
The men handed her the blueprints and left.

47
00:03:56.443 --> 00:04:01.961
"Wait!" Ally jumped up. "Were you talking about the parking lot?

48
00:04:01.962 --> 00:04:05.876
Because we collected a lot of letters and signatures on a petition.

49
00:04:05.877 --> 00:04:09.340
Lots of people want to save the soccer field."

50
00:04:09.341 --> 00:04:14.238
"I know. We're getting a lot of phone calls in support of the field.

51
00:04:14.239 --> 00:04:19.837
But I'm sorry, Ally, it's too late." Mayor Clark shook her head.

52
00:04:19.838 --> 00:04:24.185
"But the kids will lose their soccer field!" Ally said.

53
00:04:24.186 --> 00:04:27.974
The mayor shrugged sadly. "It's life, I suppose."

54
00:04:27.975 --> 00:04:33.489
She turned to go back to her office when Ally's eyes landed on the blueprints.

55
00:04:33.490 --> 00:04:39.258
"Are those the plans for the parking lot?" she asked. "May I look at them?"

56
00:04:39.259 --> 00:04:45.105
"I don't see why not." The mayor spread the blueprints out on a table.

57
00:04:45.106 --> 00:04:46.734
"Here's the parking lot.

58
00:04:46.735 --> 00:04:52.867
And we've planned for a small drive-through coffee shop so people can grab a cup of coffee on their way to work.

59
00:04:52.868 --> 00:04:56.079
I was going to ask Ray if he'd like to run it."

60
00:04:56.080 --> 00:05:00.907
Ally's eyes went wide. She had just gotten the best idea!

61
00:05:00.908 --> 00:05:04.223
"Mayor, did you know that Ray has a food truck?

62
00:05:04.224 --> 00:05:09.469
What if he agreed to serve coffee and breakfast foods every morning?

63
00:05:09.470 --> 00:05:16.424
Then you won't have to build the shop, and the parking lot could be smaller, leaving room for a field."

64
00:05:16.425 --> 00:05:18.187
The mayor frowned.

65
00:05:18.188 --> 00:05:23.204
Ally held her breath. "Please, please, please," she thought.

66
00:05:23.205 --> 00:05:27.791
"You know . . ." The mayor looked thoughtful.

67
00:05:27.792 --> 00:05:35.167
"That's not a bad idea." She rolled up the blueprints.

68
00:05:35.168 --> 00:05:38.921
"Maybe I'll speak to the developers to see what they think.

69
00:05:38.922 --> 00:05:41.819
Do you want to speak with Ray about the coffee?"

70
00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:42.875
"Of course!"

71
00:05:42.876 --> 00:05:45.694
Ally left the office and crossed her fingers.

72
00:05:45.695 --> 00:05:48.173
But it wasn't because she had told a fib.

73
00:05:48.174 --> 00:05:54.246
This time it was for luck that her plan would work!

